    "title": "Backend Developer Needed — Real-Time Multi-User App (Supabase)",
    "ciphertext": "~022078831197574511355",
    "description": "I'm building a social app where friends create private rooms, queue music together, and can pull in a live DJ. There's already a working front-end prototype built (rooms, YouTube-link queue, DJ profiles, user profiles) — I'll share the file and full technical spec with selected candidates.\n\nWhat I need for this first phase:\n- A real backend (Supabase preferred) so multiple people, each on their own device, can join the same room and see the same synced queue update live\n- Basic user accounts (email/password or magic link is enough)\n- Deployed somewhere reliable\n\nNot needed yet: payments, native live video streaming, or a mobile app.\n\nTo apply, please tell me:\n1. Have you built real-time, multi-user apps before — specifically things where multiple people see live updates together?\n2. A link to something similar you've actually shipped.\n3. Have you worked with Supabase specifically for real-time syncing between users?\n\nI'd like to start with a small, paid trial task before committing to the full scope.",
